{
  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "Evidence: The two strongest findings so far are (1) multiprofile + avgpool aggregation boosts RNA-only accuracy from 0.485 to 0.591 (config_002 vs config_001), and (2) adding image (resnet50, concat) to singleprofile RNA improves accuracy from 0.485 to 0.527 (config_016 vs config_001). However, we have not yet tested whether these two gains are additive. Question: config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat) directly combines the two proven design choices—multiprofile avgpool aggregation and concat fusion with resnet50—changing only the addition of the image modality relative to config_002. This isolates the marginal contribution of image in the multiprofile setting. Why best next: It is the most logical exploitation of the two strongest signals, uses a single-variable change from the current best (config_002), and will clarify whether the weak image-only signal (0.208) can still contribute meaningfully when paired with a strong multiprofile RNA backbone. The result will guide whether further budget should go toward better image encoders (ViT-L), alternative aggregation (transformer), or alternative fusion (weighted) in the multimodal+multiprofile regime."
}

